Used only by the tests, as the reference the phase distortion of CZumarzu is
checked against. Not compiled into the add-on.

Local changes:
- Removed the MAME device, stream, timer and IRQ glue, and the two-byte serial
  register protocol: a register is written with write(reg, value).
- Replaced u8/u16/s16/u32/s32 with the <cstdint> types and BIT() with a local
  helper of the same meaning.
- machine().rand() is a local xorshift32; noise modulation is therefore not
  the bit sequence MAME produces, only its statistics.
- update() returns the sum of the eight voices, clamped as
  stream.put_int_clamp(0, i, sample, 1 << 15) does.
- The voice processing order, transfer functions, windows, volume and pitch
  tables, envelopes and DCW limit are unchanged.

No ROMs, firmware or patch data are included.
